{
  "chapter_note": "This chunk tightly binds the I-am claims to the gospel-as-law thesis, ending with strong parallel structure and a clean handoff to the Name chapter. Voice stays dense, assertive, and law-positive with no AI padding or sentence-open violations. Scripture quotes and AsciiDoc markup are clean. Residual defects are a presenter staging cue, an incomplete idiom around 'made to sound,' and inverted phrasing that slightly blurs 'the standard walking.' No doctrine or factual mismatches appear.",
  "proposals": [
    {
      "old": "Read through the symbols, it is simply this: there has only ever been _one_ way — one covenant-conduct, one standard, one life — and it now has a name.",
      "new": "Through the symbols, it is simply this: there has only ever been _one_ way — one covenant-conduct, one standard, one life — and it now has a name.",
      "type": "ai-sounding-staging",
      "severity": "high",
      "summary": "Remove residual director cue that instructs the reader how to read.",
      "rationale": "House style bans presenter staging of the 'Read that slowly' type. The claim can stand as direct assertion without the imperative."
    },
    {
      "old": "The last line, then, is not the slammed door it is so often made to sound: __“no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.”__",
      "new": "The last line, then, is not the slammed door it is so often made to sound like: __“no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.”__",
      "type": "grammar",
      "severity": "medium",
      "summary": "Complete the incomplete idiom 'made to sound.'",
      "rationale": "English requires 'like' (or equivalent) after 'made to sound' when the following noun is the comparison. The fix restores grammar without changing force or metaphor."
    },
    {
      "old": "He is the Torah embodied — the standard walking.",
      "new": "He is the Torah embodied — the walking standard.",
      "type": "clarity",
      "severity": "medium",
      "summary": "Restore natural English order for the appositive claim.",
      "rationale": "'The standard walking' inverts expected order and can read as adjective + noun. 'The walking standard' states the same identification cleanly and keeps the density."
    }
  ]
}
